hypotheses.statement:
Assume Input <a href="#input:hecke" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="input:hecke">4</a>. For each fixed positive prime $q$, for all sufficiently large real $x$, and uniformly over primes $\ell$ with $\exp(L^{0.1})<\ell<\exp(L^{0.3})$, one has $$\#\left\{\,p\text{ prime}:
 \begin{array}{l}
 x<p<2x,\quad p\nmid q\ell,\quad p\equiv1\pmod\ell,\\
 q^{(p-1)/\ell}\equiv1\pmod p
 \end{array}\right\}
 \ll_q \frac{x}{\ell(\ell-1)L}+x^{1-\eta}.$$

Fix $\delta,C,D_*>0$ and $0<\gamma<w_-<w_+<1$. Let $F,H_m,H_n,X$ satisfy the hypotheses of Input <a href="#input:marked" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="input:marked">5</a>, including <a href="#eq:rough-dyad-range" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:rough-dyad-range">[eq:rough-dyad-range]</a>. Let $\chi_0$ be any Dirichlet character modulo the fixed $M$. On an arbitrary interval $I\subseteq[H_m,2H_m]$, put $$\label{eq:twisted-rough-coefficient}
 \alpha_m=\chi_0(m)m^{iv}\left(
   \mathbf 1_{P^-(m)>x^\gamma}
   -\frac{D_\gamma(\log m/L)}{LV(W)}\mathbf 1_{P^-(m)>W}\right),
 \qquad |v|\le L^C,$$ and set $\alpha_m=0$ outside $I$. Let $\beta$ be supported on $W$-rough integers in $[H_n,2H_n]$, with $|\beta_n|\le L^C$. Then $$\label{eq:twisted-rough-type-ii}
 \left|\sum_{m,n}\alpha_m\beta_nF(mn-1)\mathcal W(mn-1)\right|
      \ll XL^{-D_*}$$ when $K$ is sufficiently large in terms of the fixed data, independently of the particular $a_i$. The estimate is uniform in the permitted $F$, dyads, intervals, $\beta$, real $v$, and characters $\chi_0$. The implicit constant and threshold may depend on all fixed data, including $M$ and the $a_i$.

For every fixed $\vartheta>0$, $$\label{eq:marked-harmonic-bounds}
 1\le J_0\ll_K1,\qquad
 \sum_{\substack{r\in\mathcal G\\r>x^\vartheta}}
       \frac{\mathcal W(r)}r
       \ll_K\exp(-\vartheta L^{1-a_K}).$$ For $r\in\mathcal G$ with $r\le x^{0.05}$, put $$I_r=\frac{x}{4r}\int_1^2
       \frac{\Psi(u)}{\log((xu-1)/(4r))}\,\mathrm du.$$ For every fixed $A>0$, uniformly in these $r$, $$\label{eq:progression-pnt}
 A_r=\frac{I_r}{\varphi(M)}+O_{M,\Psi,A}\left(\frac xr L^{-A}\right),
 \qquad I_r\asymp_\Psi\frac{x}{rL}.$$ Furthermore, $$\label{eq:marked-mass-comparability}
 X_0\asymp_{M,\Psi}\frac{xJ_0}{L}.$$ The comparison constants here can be chosen independently of $K$ and the $a_i$; the threshold for $x$ may depend on them. For every fixed $\vartheta,A>0$, $$\label{eq:marked-tail}
 \sum_{\substack{r\in\mathcal G\\r>x^\vartheta}}
       \mathcal W(r)A_r=o(X_0L^{-A}).$$

For every fixed $A>0$, $$\label{eq:averaged-distribution}
 \sum_{\substack{r\in\mathcal G\\r\le x^\epsilon}}\mathcal W(r)
 \sum_{\substack{\ell\le D_0\text{ odd and squarefree}\\
                  \gcd(\ell,M)=1}}
       |R_r(\ell)|\ll xJ_0L^{-A}.$$ The constant and threshold may depend on the fixed parameters.

